{"id": "EUVD-2026-80471", "enisaUuid": "7a317d0a-157a-3a47-8186-9375c4d9dbd5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: video-i2c: fix kthread error pointer left in kthread_vid_cap on failure\n\nkthread_run() returns an ERR_PTR on failure, not NULL.\nWhen start_streaming() fails, data->kthread_vid_cap is left holding\nthis error pointer instead of being cleared.\n\nThis causes two subsequent bugs:\n1. A future call to start_streaming() sees a non-NULL kthread_vid_cap\n   and returns 0 (success) immediately, without actually starting the\n   capture thread.\n2. A call to stop_streaming() checks 'kthread_vid_cap == NULL' which\n   is false for an error pointer, and proceeds to call kthread_stop()\n   on the error pointer, leading to a kernel crash.\n\nFix this by resetting kthread_vid_cap to NULL on failure before\njumping to the error path.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:54:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db0f4531aa55cfb0171684ebfffe3ff04b79d5a8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0fac63cac6689588da530764ccb6ba55ee8e4d8b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5c35d380bea60503c4fe0986fe1de6a3263282b3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d1b10d81fe54852ed953f4129577b733bbd6907", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/968c5213e34c48d35febdfd09cf3dc58ad039140", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/52fd9d80c0cea7bf09e7ee36cad316e5c39b7fe6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e7f2cd72a4f9268ee09a13b13f3339e7cc71557", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/76e379754ba618989f6215be608d5c04774a611d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89871", "GHSA-5fv9-jv39-xhgw"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ff35af6-d840-3468-a038-5be73a922887", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5cebaac609744414463d1ecc28fdecd26c1b9bc1 <76e379754ba618989f6215be608d5c04774a611d"}, {"id": "1d1e7653-b542-320c-902a-b628af0c5eec", "produ